# Rover P6 2200 four-door saloon, 1973-1977.
#
# The 2.2-litre four P6 introduced with the 1973 range: the same de Dion rear
# end and base-unit body as the 2000, with the larger engine and the TC trim.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rover_P6
#
# Dimensions 4.572 x 1.676 x 1.422 m, wheelbase 2.616 m (family figures).
#
# Shape reference: no true level side elevation exists. Image 1 is identified
# as a TC by the Commons title and the wing trim; the front and rear views
# show different variants. The flank is estimated; the limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: no model-specific UK chart was established. Arden Green, Davos
# White, Squadron Blue and Mexico Brown are documented Rover finishes of the
# period. Weights 25, 22, 18, 15, total 80, provisional.
#
# Speed 165 km/h. Comfort 110/495, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 110, the same
# P6 cabin as the 2000. Classes 2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 1973 intro, retires staggered 1990-1993.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rover-p6-2200.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/rover-p6-2200.dae. References:
# citycars/references/rover-p6-2200/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: there is no true side elevation; image 1 is a TC at an
# angle and the front and rear views show different variants. The flank is
# estimated, and the build is a simplified adaptation of the existing P6 2000
# master. At 128 px the P6 base-unit body and 2200 trim read as a P6 2200.


obj=citycar
name=RoverP62200(ArdenGreen)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=25
intro_year=1973
intro_month=10
retire_year=1993
retire_month=6
speed=165
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=110
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=495

